Both the dynamic `import()` and the Prisma query can reject (module resolution failure, connection pool exhaustion, DB outage). The promise is not awaited inside a try/catch, so the rejection propagates out of this authorization helper. In the current callers the route handler's top-level await will surface as an unhandled 500 rather than a controlled response, and in a context where the result is consumed in a boolean expression (like the admin `page.tsx`) the failure mode is easy to mis-handle. Wrap the lookup and fail closed, e.g.:
```ts
try {
  const { getPrismaClient } = await import("@/lib/server/prisma");
  const prisma = getPrismaClient();
  if (!prisma) return false;
  return Boolean(await prisma.activityCommunityMember.findFirst({ ... }));
} catch {
  return false; // fail closed on infrastructure errors
}
```
Note that returning `false` on infrastructure failure masks outages as permission denials; log the error so it stays observable.

